To meet the requirements of adding a "test" button to the `PluginCard` component and handling events with `PluginModal`, let's update the components accordingly.

### `PluginCard.vue` Update
We'll add the "test" button that, when clicked, will trigger the display of the `PluginModal`. The button will listen for the "save" event and process the arguments accordingly.

```vue /home/codx-junior-projects/codx-junior/client/src/components/global_settings/plugins/PluginCard.vue
<script setup>
</script>

<template>
  <div class="card shadow hover:shadow-lg cursor-pointer bg-base-100 border">
    <div class="card-body flex flex-col">
      <h2 class="card-title">{{ plugin.name }}</h2>
      <p>{{ plugin.description }}</p>
      <div class="grow"></div>
      <div>
        {{ plugin.extends.join(',') }}
      </div>
      <button @click="toggleModal" class="btn btn-primary mt-2">Test</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <PluginModal v-if="showModal" :plugin="plugin" @save="handleSave" @remove="removePlugin" />
</template>

<script>
export default {
  props: ['plugin'],
  data() {
    return {
      showModal: false,
    }
  },
  methods: {
    toggleModal() {
      this.showModal = !this.showModal
    },
    handleSave(argumentsData) {
      // Construct dictionary from arguments
      const argumentDict = argumentsData.reduce((acc, arg) => {
        acc[arg.name] = arg.default_value
        return acc
      }, {})
      this.$emit('test', argumentDict)
      this.showModal = false
    },
    removePlugin() {
      // Handle plugin removal if needed
    }
  }
}
</script>
```

### `PluginModal.vue` Update
We will make sure `PluginModal` is capable of emitting a "save" event with the argument data.

```vue /home/codx-junior-projects/codx-junior/client/src/components/global_settings/plugins/PluginModal.vue
<script setup>
</script>

<template>
  <div class="flex flex-col gap-2 p-4">
    <h2 class="text-lg font-bold mb-2">{{ plugin.name }}</h2>
    <div v-for="arg in editablePlugin.arguments" :key="arg.name" class="mb-2">
      <div class="block" v-text="arg.name"></div>
      <input v-model="arg.default_value" type="text" class="input input-bordered w-full" />
    </div>
    <div class="modal-action">
      <button @click="saveChanges" class="btn btn-sm btn-success">Save Changes</button>
      <button @click="removePlugin" class="btn btn-sm btn-error">{{ confirmDeletion ? "Confirm Deletion?" : "Delete" }}</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</template>

<script>
export default {
  props: ['plugin'],
  data() {
    return {
      editablePlugin: { ...this.plugin },
      confirmDeletion: false,
    }
  },
  methods: {
    saveChanges() {
      this.$emit('save', this.editablePlugin.arguments)
    },
    removePlugin() {
      if (this.confirmDeletion) {
        this.$emit('remove')
      } else {
        this.confirmDeletion = true
      }
    }
  }
}
</script>
```

### Notes
- The `PluginCard` now shows a modal with editable plugin arguments when the "test" button is clicked.
- After editing, clicking "Save Changes" in the modal will send the argument data back to `PluginCard`, which constructs a dictionary and emits a "test" event.
- The updates maintain consistency with the project's use of Vue.js and TailwindCSS structure.
